# Copy to .env (it is in .gitignore). Everything here is optional.

# Port and address the bridge listens on. Default 5400 on all interfaces.
# PORT=5400
# BIND_HOST=0.0.0.0

# Wake-on-LAN broadcast address, if the TV does not wake. Your subnet's broadcast, e.g. x.x.x.255.
# TV_BROADCAST=255.255.255.255

# Where the claude program lives, if it is not on the PATH (only for the optional Ask feature).
# CLAUDE_BIN=/usr/local/bin/claude

# Use a different config file, data folder or ADB key.
# COUCH_CONFIG=/path/to/config.json
# COUCH_DATA=/path/to/data
# ADB_KEY=~/.android/adbkey

# Do NOT put ANTHROPIC_API_KEY here. The Ask feature runs `claude -p` on your own Claude plan and
# strips that variable before it starts, so an API key never gets used (and never gets billed).

# Smart home (optional, docs/CONFIG.md): the long-lived access token of a Home Assistant user made
# just for the TV. Only used when config.json has a home_assistant section; apply.sh hands it to
# the TV app, which keeps it in its own private storage.
# HOME_ASSISTANT_TOKEN=
